  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1.2. Increased institutional capacity of workers&#x2019; organizations</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The National Trade Union Confederation of Moldova (CNSM) developed a new strategy document that was adopted during their Congress in June 2022. The strategy calls for increased relevance of workers and aims at attracting new members. 

Following the successful development in North Macedonia of a phone application for workers to report labour rights violations directly to the trade union, the CNSM introduced the same service in Moldova in July 2022. The application &#x201C;Workers&#x2019; Rights&#x201D; is a user-friendly tool informing about changes in labour legislation, occupational safety and health regulations, or social insurance matters as well as trade union services. Subscribers receive notifications from trade unions with news and latest developments. Two weeks after the launch, about 3,000 unique users visited the application, and roughly 400 people downloaded it. In both North Macedonia and Moldova, the application will be linked to the State Labour Inspectorate. 

Following the war in Ukraine, in February 2022 the National Trade Union Confederation of Moldova has also provided 18.000 bed-nights for refugees. The ILO provided support to the CNSM to develop the new strategy in 2022 through sharing of expertise and best-case examples from other countries. This included particularly the opportunity to coordinate with and learn from Romanian trade unions. In July 2022, ILO supported a study visit by CNSM to Romanian national centre trade unions. The study visit focussed on:

- aspects of European social law;
-the social dimension of the European integration of the Republic of Moldova;
-the role of trade Union structures in promoting social partnership;
- EU Directives in the field of labour, equal opportunities, Safety and Health at work (OSH);
- the role of trade unions in monitoring their implementation;
- the refugee crisis, generated by the war in Ukraine, and the involvement of trade unions in the management and protection of refugees;
- strengthening the capacities of trade union structures in the Republic of Moldova in the process of European integration

The ILO did also provide capacity development meetings for CNSM leadership and staff in 2nd quarter of 2023 on how to use the new phone application. 

To provide emergency accommodation for refugees from Ukraine, the ILO assisted the CNSM with financial aid. The service was provided to refugees free of charge.</narrative>
   </description>
